dialect protocol
protocol binary.diff
version 1
schema stdio.binary
start pack

# P2-P3: real binary diff frame -- CONFIRMED ALREADY REAL, not a text-as-binary shortcut needing
# upgrade. `BinaryDiff { splices: Vec<ByteSplice> }` is a plain struct with zero `Option<Option<T>>`
# tri-state fields and zero data-carrying enums anywhere in its type tree (`ByteSplice` itself is
# `#[derive(dsl::DslRecord)]`) -- per this program's own F6 finding, this is the ONE clean
# full-derive-path success in the entire 31-standard program. `#[derive(dsl::DslDiff)]`'s generated
# `DiffCodec::encode_diff`/`decode_diff` (`✨️derive/🦀️.rs`'s `derive_dsl_diff`) route
# through `store::pack_rt::encode_document`/`decode_document` -- NOT the lightweight container-less
# `encode_record_body` the sibling mutations facet uses, but the FULL `.spk` binary document
# container (magic + 32-byte header + a sequence of framed, individually-CRC'd, deflate-compressed
# segments + a fixed 84-byte footer), confirmed by direct read of both the derive macro and
# `🎒️pack/📐️format/🦀️.rs`'s own module doc ("the `SPK` binary document container"). This
# EXACT layout (magic `0x8953504B0D0A1A0A`, `header fixed 24`, a repeated tag-dispatched segment
# block, `footer fixed 84`) is the framework's own canonical worked example for this dialect
# (`📖️grammar/🦀️.rs`'s `protocol_parse_print_round_trip_retains_body`/
# `protocol_parses_rich_struct_enum_segment_forms` tests use the identical magic/header-size/
# footer-size triple) -- restated here honestly rather than assumed, since cross-artifact `use` to
# point at a shared framework-level description does not yet resolve at walk time (P2-M3, same
# documented limitation as the `semio.envelope` file every OTHER artifact's snapshot pack facet
# would otherwise want to `use`).
#
# Segment frame (`encode_segment`, `🎒️pack/📐️format/🦀️.rs`): `kind u8, flags u8, seg_len
# varint, [raw_len varint if compressed], payload (seg_len bytes, deflate-compressed when
# `flags==3`), crc32 u32`. `encode_document` (called with `PackEncodeOptions::default()`,
# `codec: CodecId(1)` = deflate) ALWAYS writes exactly this sequence of segment kinds for a diff
# this small (confirmed by direct observation of real `encode_diff()` output, byte for byte):
# `KIND_SYMBOLS=3` (flags=3, compressed), `KIND_DOCUMENT=4` (flags=3), `KIND_MANIFEST=1` (flags=3),
# `KIND_END=0` (flags=0, the repeat's own sentinel -- `encode_segment(KIND_END, CodecId(0), &[])`
# is always uncompressed by construction). All four arms share the identical field shape below
# (kind is the only real discriminator); the `if flags eq 3` guard on `raw_len` is real and
# structural (matches `decode_segment_at`'s own `compressed = flags & 0x01 != 0` check), not just
# true empirically for this artifact's fixtures. Segment PAYLOAD bytes are deflate-compressed --
# an honest opaque boundary at the protocol-description level, the same documented treatment this
# program gives every other compressed byte run (zlib/deflate container payloads, PNG IDAT, ...);
# the Rust `encode_diff`/`decode_diff` side IS genuinely, fully structured real binary (round-trip
# tested independently, see this artifact's `diff_codec_text_binary_roundtrip_law`). The 84-byte
# footer (magic `SPKFOOT1` + version + flags + manifest offset/len + file_len + a 32-byte content
# hash + prev-footer-offset + its own crc32) is likewise one opaque fixed trailer at this
# description layer -- `Block::Footer` has no field-level detail in this dialect at all (same
# honest-boundary treatment as PDF/DWG's own undecoded regions), its real field layout stays
# Rust-side in `🎒️pack/📐️format/🦀️.rs`'s `Footer::parse`/`write_bytes`.
framing magic 0x8953504B0D0A1A0A
header fixed 24
field version_major u16
field version_minor u16
field required_flags u32
field optional_flags u32
field header_crc32 u32
field reserved fixed 8

repeat segments {
  tag u8
  trailer u32
  until 0
  arm 3 { flags u8 seg_len varint raw_len varint if flags eq 3 payload Array(u8, Field(seg_len)) }
  arm 4 { flags u8 seg_len varint raw_len varint if flags eq 3 payload Array(u8, Field(seg_len)) }
  arm 1 { flags u8 seg_len varint raw_len varint if flags eq 3 payload Array(u8, Field(seg_len)) }
  arm 0 { flags u8 seg_len varint raw_len varint if flags eq 3 payload Array(u8, Field(seg_len)) }
}

footer fixed 84
